/data/

# vercel
.vercel

# SpacetimeDB
# NOTE: /src/module_bindings/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It was, on the grounds
# that stale copies in a diff are worse than no copies — true for local work, and
# fatal for deployment: the app imports the bindings, Vercel has no `spacetime`
# CLI to produce them, so `next build` cannot resolve `@/module_bindings` and the
# deploy fails. Committing them is what makes the build reproducible off a clean
# clone. The staleness risk is now a review discipline: regenerate with
# `npm run stdb:generate` after any schema change, and commit the result with it.
#
# The module's own build output is the opposite case, and was tracked by mistake.
# `spacetime build`, `publish` and `generate` all bundle from --module-path source,
# so nothing ever reads this file back — and Vercel does not build the module at
# all. Tracked, it did two bad things: rewrote itself on every local build so a
# `git pull --rebase` refused to run, and sat 2MB stale in every diff, because
# whoever last committed it had run a build and nobody since had.
/spacetimedb/dist/
# Which database this checkout publishes to, per developer.
/spacetime.local.json

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Vendored agent skills, installed by `uipro init` rather than written here.
# ~3MB of CSV databases and Python, six of the seven unrelated to this project.
# They work the same installed locally; keeping them out of the repo keeps a clone small.
# Everything else under .claude/skills/ IS ours and stays tracked.
/.claude/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/
/.claude/skills/banner-design/
/.claude/skills/brand/
/.claude/skills/design/
/.claude/skills/design-system/
/.claude/skills/slides/
/.claude/skills/ui-styling/

